Power BI Project: Zepto Inventory Dashboard

1. Project Objective
The objective of this project is to analyze inventory availability, pricing, discounts, and product weight to:
Monitor product availability
Track discount performance
Compare MRP vs Selling Price
Identify out-of-stock products
Analyze inventory quantity and weight distribution

This dashboard helps retail managers and store owners make better pricing and stock decisions.

2. Dataset Description
The dataset contains product-level inventory and pricing details.

Column	Description
Category	Product category
Name	Product name
MRP	Maximum Retail Price
DiscountPercent	Discount offered
AvailableQuantity	Available stock
DiscountedSellingPrice	Final selling price
WeightInGms	Product weight
OutOfStock	Product availability status
Quantity	Product unit quantity

3. Data Cleaning in Power BI
Steps performed in Power Query Editor:
Imported Excel dataset
Checked data types
Removed duplicate rows
Handled missing values
Converted:
Price columns → Currency
Weight → Numeric
Verified OutOfStock Boolean values

4. Data Modeling
No complex relationships were required since it is a single-table dataset.
However, calculated fields were created.

Calculated Columns
1. Discount Amount
Discount Amount = [MRP] - [discountedSellingPrice]
2. Discount Value %
Discount Value % = 
DIVIDE([Discount Amount],[MRP]) * 100
3. Stock Status
Stock Status =
IF([outOfStock] = TRUE(), "Out of Stock", "Available")

5. Key KPIs for Dashboard
Add Card Visuals:
1️⃣ Total Products
Total Products = COUNT(name)

2️⃣ Total Available Quantity
Total Stock = SUM(availableQuantity)

3️⃣ Average Discount
Avg Discount = AVERAGE(discountPercent)

4️⃣ Total Inventory Weight
Total Weight = SUM(weightInGms)

5️⃣ Out of Stock Products
Out of Stock Count =
CALCULATE(COUNT(name), outOfStock = TRUE())


